SEC. 51P-576.103. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATIONS.

(a) Unless otherwise stated, the definitions and interpretations in Chapter 51A apply to this article. In this article:

(1) ASSISTED LIVING FACILITY means an interim or permanent residential facility which furnishes food, shelter, laundry, and other assistance in activities of daily living to five or more persons, age 55 or older, who are not related by blood, marriage, or adoption to the owner or proprietor of the establishment. Food is prepared in a central kitchen. Assisted living facilities must be licensed as assisted living facilities under Chapter 247 of the Texas Health and Safety Code. This use does not include:

(A) other licensed health facilities under Subtitle B, “Licensing of Health Facilities,” of the Texas Health and Safety Code, specifically convalescent and nursing homes and related institutions;

(B) facilities that negotiate sleeping arrangements on a daily basis;

(C) dwelling units occupied by families (note: dwelling units occupied exclusively by families are considered to be single family, duplex, or multifamily uses as the case may be);

(D) halfway houses; and

(E) overnight general purpose shelters.

(b) Unless otherwise stated, all code references are to Chapter 51A.

(c) This district is considered to be a residential zoning district. (Ord. Nos. 24266; 25163)
